<div class="marquee" aria-label="News"><span>*** 2026-09-30: spec2 drafted *** Now working on P1: first pixels on screen &amp; PCI device listing *** No BIOS required ***</span></div>

<p style="margin-top:14px"><span class="wmbox"><img class="wmimg" src="/assets/img/wordmark.png" width="294" height="124" alt="LWOS: Every byte by hand."></span></p>

<hr>

<h2 id="about"><img src="/assets/gif/spin.gif" alt="">What is LWOS?</h2>
<p>A hobby operating system for CNC milling machines. It looks and feels like an IBM PC, but it doesn't depend on the BIOS.</p>
<figure class="crt"><img src="/assets/gif/boot.gif" width="640" height="288" alt="LWOS loader reading FAT32, then the MONITOR prompt"><figcaption>From power-on to the MONITOR prompt (illustration)</figcaption></figure>
<p class="ucrow"><img src="/assets/gif/construction.gif" width="140" height="44" alt="Under construction"><span><b>UNDER CONSTRUCTION</b><br>v2 is an early rewrite. APIs and layout may change without notice.</span></p>

<hr>

<h2 id="memory">Flat memory, hardware tasks</h2>
<p>No paging and no page tables. Everything lives in one flat 4&nbsp;GB address space, so a C pointer is a physical address you can hand straight to a DMA engine. Each task gets a TSS descriptor in the GDT, and the timer switches between them with a far jump.</p>
<figure class="crt"><img src="/assets/gif/flatmem.gif" width="560" height="336" alt="Memory map from 0 to 4 GB beside the GDT; the timer jumps between TSS entries for MONITOR, task A and task B"><figcaption>One address space, three tasks, no walls. Multitasking is planned for P7 (illustration)</figcaption></figure>

<hr>

<h2 id="works">What works today <img src="/assets/gif/new.gif" width="40" height="16" alt="NEW!" style="vertical-align:middle;margin-left:6px"></h2>
<ul class="links plain">
  <li>MBR boot with partition table</li>
  <li>Read-only FAT32 in the loader</li>
  <li><code>mkfat</code>, a host tool for building FAT images</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-top:8px">Coming next: a <code>DEBUG.COM</code>-style monitor, an <code>EDIT.COM</code>-style editor, and the CNC stack.</p>

<hr>

<h2 id="build">Build &amp; run</h2>
<p>You need <code>make</code>, a C compiler, and <a href={QEMU}>QEMU</a> or <a href={BOCHS}>Bochs</a>.</p>
<div class="scroll-x"><pre>git clone {REPO}
cd lwos
make run</pre></div>
<p><a class="btn95" href={REPO}>Get the source...</a> <a class="btn95" href={WIKI}>Read the wiki</a></p>

